Subject: remote_debug.h: terminate the path proc_regionfilename() returns

On Mac OS X 10.9, proc_regionfilename() copies the region's path into the
buffer and returns its length without writing a NUL. search_map_for_section()
then reads its uninitialized stack buffer as a C string, so the file name it
matches against "libpython"/"python" and the path it opens both carry
whatever bytes follow, and every remote debugging call on a live process
(sys.remote_exec, _remote_debugging's GCMonitor) fails with "Failed to find
the PyRuntime section". The returned length is authoritative, so the path
ends there.

Upstreamable as is. Drop it when CPython terminates the path itself.

--- a/Python/remote_debug.h
+++ b/Python/remote_debug.h
@@ -624,6 +624,7 @@
             address += size;
             continue;
         }
+        map_filename[path_len] = '\0';
 
         char* filename = strrchr(map_filename, '/');
         if (filename != NULL) {
